<h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="usa-accordion usa-accordion--bordered usa-accordion--multiselectable" data-allow-multiple="">
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-1">What is a pallet conveyor?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-1" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>A pallet conveyor is a heavy-duty material handling system that transports loaded or empty pallets through packaging, warehousing, and manufacturing operations. Pallet conveyors use <a href="/conveyor-types/cdlr-conveyors/">chain-driven live rollers (CDLR)</a>, drag chains, or heavy-duty powered rollers to move loads from empty pallet stacks to heavy beverage and drum pallets.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">How much weight can a pallet conveyor handle?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-2" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>It depends on the model, and capacity is rated per linear foot and per zone. Hytrol, for example, rates its CDLR models from 250 lb/ft (199-CRR) to 2,000 lb/ft (36-CRRH) and its drag chain models at 3,000 to 4,000 lb per zone. Light duty carries empty pallets, standard duty carries typical loaded GMA pallets, and heavy duty carries beverage, drum, and industrial loads.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">What is the difference between CDLR and drag chain pallet conveyors?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-3" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p><strong>CDLR</strong> uses chain-driven steel rollers. Pallets ride on the rollers. CDLR supports zoned accumulation. It is the most common pallet conveyor type.</p>
<p><strong>Drag chain</strong> uses strands of chain running in tracks. Pallets ride directly on the chain. Drag chain suits heavy loads and non-standard pallet sizes but does not support accumulation without separate drive zones.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">How do pallet conveyors integrate with stretch wrappers?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-4" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Turntable wrappers use chain transfers to move pallets on/off the turntable. Rotary arm wrappers keep the pallet on the conveyor while the wrapping arm rotates around it. The conveyor stages pallets upstream of the wrapper to prevent the palletizer from stopping during the wrap cycle.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-5">What speed do pallet conveyors run at?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-5" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Pallet conveyors run much slower than case conveyors. Set speed from the palletizer and stretch wrapper cycle times: the discharge conveyor must clear a finished pallet before the next one is complete. Running faster than needed adds load shift risk without adding throughput.</p>

</div>
</div>
